     "<div lang=\"EN-AU\" link=\"blue\" vlink=\"purple\"><div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><b><span lang=\"EN-US\">From:</span></b><span lang=\"EN-US\"> <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">da...@googlegroups.com</a> &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">da...@googlegroups.com</a>&gt;\r\n<b>On Behalf Of </b>Neutronstar21<br>\r\n<b>Sent:</b> Tuesday, 12 April 2022 12:36<br>\r\n<b>To:</b> dartR &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">da...@googlegroups.com</a>&gt;<br>\r\n<b>Subject:</b> [dartR] the new gl2genepop() is excellent!<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Thanks so much for putting this converter in. The genepop format is so widely used.<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">However, it would be very useful to have a parameter option that forces the pops to be written out in a predetermined order<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">something like:<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">pop_order_list = c(Z, X, Y)<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Thanks again for dartR!<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Cheers,<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Dean<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div></div>"
